11.0.0 — strum and voicings for your chords, your own click, white balance for video takes, and finer editing

New since 10082, built by the Echoel Studio run; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Note editor, Chords menu: Strum spreads each chord down (lowest note first) or up over a 1/128,
  1/64 or 1/32 note; every note still ends where it ended; Together puts it back. Voicing moves one
  note of each chord an octave: Invert Up, Invert Down, Open, Drop 2, Drop 3. On the chosen note's
  chord, or every chord; one Undo each. Nothing is added.
- Note editor: in a song with a key, the rows of the scale are lit a little and the root's a little
  more; the side keyboard marks the root with a dot and the other scale tones with a ring.
- Click Sound (Click key's hold menu, or More): Built-in Click or Choose Sound… — an audio file up
  to 10 s; its first 0.2 s plays on every beat and in the count-in, at the click's level. Kept on
  this device, never in a song.
- Camera take: White Balance — Auto, 3200, 4000, 5600, 6500 or 7500 K, held through a lens change.
- Browser: a video has Watch; its picture plays at the top of the list, muted and looping, until Stop.
- Automation lanes: a double tap removes a point or straightens a bend (a single tap only adds a
  point); points follow the song's magnet grid instead of a fixed sixteenth. With VoiceOver a lane
  has Add Point at Playhead, Delete Point at Playhead, and swipe up or down moves that point.
- Region settings: Gain in tenths of a dB; each gain or fade change is its own Undo; Halve and
  Double next to Native Tempo.
Limits, new: above 300 BPM a sample click is cut by the next one; a video's sound is not heard in
the browser; the app does not read Bold Text yet.
Older limits as in 10082.

Previous: 10082. A green commit that changes this file uploads build 10000 + run number. A test
list, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

One ask, as for 10081 and 10082. Start a screen recording, open the app, and try to make sixteen
bars in two to five minutes: a beat, a bass line or a chord, then Play. No list and no protocol;
stop wherever it stops being possible or pleasant. The recording is the answer. What gets in the
way in it is the next work, in the order it happened.

The five checks of 10079 stay open and unchanged and rest until that recording exists.
